Previous evidence: [{"round": 0, "recipe": {"schema_version": "fk-robot-part-v1", "zone_sha256": "b6e92b2a80c9501f6ae1aea3c52e5d584e8df5a18f9981e0207d796cb7f12c49", "name": "duckling_crest_puff", "rationale": "Plan revision after attempt-0 rejection: bilateral source features must use Y>=0 only; the pair member at Y=-3.5 was illegal. Removed it — the host mirrors the remaining Y>=0 puff across Y=0, restoring the same three-puff silhouette. Center puff at [0,0,4.5] tilted back -15deg overlaps the 14x12x2.5 base positively; side puff at [ -1.5, 3.5, 5.5] with half-extents <=3 mm keeps lowest Z ~2.5mm>0 even with -25deg tilt, overlapping the base in XY. All geometry stays well inside the 80x80x35 mm zone; soft ellipsoids avoid sharp intimidating silhouettes per the friendly-duckling brief. Camera lens on the head front and all source geometry untouched; adhesive-pad attachment and walking/printability remain open.", "symmetry": "bilateral", "material": "pla", "color_rgb": [1.0, 0.72, 0.2], "base_size_mm": [14.0, 12.0, 2.5], "features": [{"shape": "ellipsoid", "size_mm": [10.0, 8.0, 6.0], "center_mm": [0.0, 0.0, 4.5], "rotation_deg": [-15.0, 0.0, 0.0]}, {"shape": "ellipsoid", "size_mm": [8.0, 5.0, 5.0], "center_mm": [-1.5, 3.5, 5.5], "rotation_deg": [-25.0, -20.0, 10.0]}]}, "review": {"recipe_sha256": "47de11472e44efcaba67d3dd13883d7764d2f1c8a084a533835950e425600c8b", "verdict": "needs-review", "findings": ["Build is host-eligible: proof accepted, motion passed at all 31 poses with min distance 16.8 mm, single fused solid, added mass 0.88 g — no floating or disconnected geometry in the CAD facts.", "Close-up renders show the crest sits cleanly on the head-top rear slope, forward of the rear edge, and does not intrude on the camera lens or front dome in any of the four views.", "Problem: at 14x12x2.5 base with 6-8 mm puffs, the part reads as a tiny yellow speck in the whole-robot views (barely visible in perspective and -Y view). It fails the brief's '有辨识度' (recognizable) requirement — the silhouette is too timid relative to the large head dome.", "The three-puff 'duckling tuft' idea is coherent and friendly (no sharp edges), but at this scale it reads as a generic bump rather than a crest; the top view shows it as a small dot far from the head apex, weakening the identity claim.", "No obstruction found: the part is far from the lens (front of head) and clear of all source geometry; zone compliance confirmed by bbox within 80x80x35 mm.", "Revision direction: scale the puff cluster up modestly (center puff ~14x11x9 mm) and shift it closer to the head apex so it is clearly visible from front and side views, while keeping lowest-Z overlap with the 2.5 mm base and staying soft/rounded per the friendly brief.", "Attachment remains an adhesive-pad proposal only; interface_status is unverified and walking/printability remain open, as the brief acknowledges."], "next_step": "revise", "reason": "The candidate is structurally sound, connected and non-obstructive, and its friendly rounded styling matches the brief. However, the whole-robot renders show it is far too small and rear-placed to be recognizable as an identity feature on the XGO Duck's large head — it reads as a barely visible speck. A limited revision will enlarge and reposition the puff cluster for presence while preserving the accepted overlap, zone and motion-clearance margins."}}, {"round": 1, "state": "rejected", "attempts": [{"attempt": 0, "state": "rejected", "error": "Part CAD rejected: ValueError: Null TopoDS_Shape object", "proposed_recipe": {"schema_version": "fk-robot-part-v1", "zone_sha256": "b6e92b2a80c9501f6ae1aea3c52e5d584e8df5a18f9981e0207d796cb7f12c49", "name": "duckling_crest_puff_mk2", "rationale": "Revision after round-0 needs-review (recipe 47de1147…): renders show the crest is host-eligible but reads as a tiny yellow speck far from the head apex. Fix: enlarge the puff cluster and broaden the base for presence. Base grows 14x12x2.5 -> 18x16x3; center puff grows to 16x13x11 at [0,0,5.5] tilted back -15deg (lowest Z ~5.5-5.4~0.1, inside base thickness with full XY overlap). Two side puffs (bilateral, Y=+4 only, host mirrors) at [-2.5,4,6] sized 10x6x7 tilted back -25deg keep lowest Z ~1.8mm>0 and overlap the base in XY. Total silhouette roughly doubles in apparent area while staying soft, rounded ellipsoids with no sharp edges; mass stays far under 16 g and the 18x16 footprint plus ~11 mm height sits well inside the 80x80x35 mm zone. Part stays rear-of-apex on the head-top slope, clear of the front camera lens and dome seen in the +X and perspective views. Adhesive-pad attachment, curvature fit, printability and walking remain open per the brief.", "symmetry": "bilateral", "material": "pla", "color_rgb": [1.0, 0.72, 0.2], "base_size_mm": [18.0, 16.0, 3.0], "features": [{"shape": "ellipsoid", "size_mm": [16.0, 13.0, 11.0], "center_mm": [0.0, 0.0, 5.5], "rotation_deg": [-15.0, 0.0, 0.0]}, {"shape": "ellipsoid", "size_mm": [10.0, 6.0, 7.0], "center_mm": [-2.5, 4.0, 6.0], "rotation_deg": [-25.0, -20.0, 10.0]}, {"shape": "ellipsoid", "size_mm": [7.0, 5.0, 5.0], "center_mm": [4.0, 3.0, 4.5], "rotation_deg": [20.0, 15.0, 0.0]}]}}, {"attempt": 1, "state": "rejected", "error": "STEP volume 1946.9672945001369 differs from generating CAD 1962.304377482516", "proposed_recipe": {"schema_version": "fk-robot-part-v1", "zone_sha256": "b6e92b2a80c9501f6ae1aea3c52e5d584e8df5a18f9981e0207d796cb7f12c49", "name": "duckling_crest_puff_mk2", "rationale": "Revision after round-0 needs-review (recipe 47de1147…): renders confirm the crest is connected and non-obstructive but reads as a tiny speck; attempt-0 failed in CAD. Diagnosis of attempt-0: the 16x13x11 center puff tilted -15deg has a rotated Z half-extent of ~7.4 mm about center z=5.5, driving its lowest Z to ~-1.9 mm — below Z=0, invalid. Fix: keep the enlarged friendly silhouette but tilt the center puff only -10deg and raise it to z=7 (lowest Z ~+0.19 mm, inside the 3 mm base with full XY overlap, positive volume). Side puff (Y=+4 only, host mirrors bilaterally) raised to z=6 with milder rotations, lowest Z ~+1.4 mm, overlapping the 18x16 base in XY. Front accent puff at [4,3,5] with gentle 10deg tilt keeps lowest Z ~+1.9 mm. No feature reaches below Z=0; whole part ~18x16x~13 mm sits well inside 80x80x35 mm, mass far under 16 g. Soft rounded ellipsoid tuft, no sharp silhouettes; clear of the front camera lens and dome seen in +X and perspective views. Adhesive-pad attachment, curvature fit, printability and walking remain open per the brief.", "symmetry": "bilateral", "material": "pla", "color_rgb": [1.0, 0.72, 0.2], "base_size_mm": [18.0, 16.0, 3.0], "features": [{"shape": "ellipsoid", "size_mm": [16.0, 13.0, 11.0], "center_mm": [0.0, 0.0, 7.0], "rotation_deg": [-10.0, 0.0, 0.0]}, {"shape": "ellipsoid", "size_mm": [10.0, 6.0, 7.0], "center_mm": [-2.5, 4.0, 6.0], "rotation_deg": [-15.0, -12.0, 8.0]}, {"shape": "ellipsoid", "size_mm": [7.0, 5.0, 5.0], "center_mm": [4.0, 3.0, 5.0], "rotation_deg": [10.0, 8.0, 0.0]}]}}]}]
Rejected attempt: {"attempt": 0, "state": "rejected", "error": "STEP volume 1759.9752326865964 differs from generating CAD 1777.485359670738", "proposed_recipe": {"schema_version": "fk-robot-part-v1", "zone_sha256": "b6e92b2a80c9501f6ae1aea3c52e5d584e8df5a18f9981e0207d796cb7f12c49", "name": "duckling_crest_puff_mk2b", "rationale": "Round-1 diagnosis: attempt-0 hit a null-shape CAD failure; attempt-1's recipe (47de lineage) was geometrically valid (all lowest-Z values positive and inside the 3 mm base: center puff ~+0.19 mm, side ~+1.4 mm, front ~+1.9 mm) but was rejected on a STEP-vs-CAD volume mismatch of ~0.8%, likely a tolerance/boolean artifact. Revision: resubmit the accepted enlarged friendly three-puff silhouette with slight size adjustments (center puff 15x12x10 at z=6.8, -10deg tilt, lowest Z ~0.1 mm fully inside the base; side puffs 10x6x7 at [-2.5,4,6], mirrored from Y>=0; front accent 7x5x5 at [4,3,5]) and a simpler rotation set to reduce boolean complexity. Renders confirm the round-0 crest was connected, clear of the camera lens and front dome, and merely too small; this keeps the doubled presence while staying soft, rounded and well inside 80x80x35 mm and 16 g. Adhesive attachment, curvature fit, printability and walking remain open per the brief.", "symmetry": "bilateral", "material": "pla", "color_rgb": [1.0, 0.72, 0.2], "base_size_mm": [18.0, 16.0, 3.0], "features": [{"shape": "ellipsoid", "size_mm": [15.0, 12.0, 10.0], "center_mm": [0.0, 0.0, 6.8], "rotation_deg": [-10.0, 0.0, 0.0]}, {"shape": "ellipsoid", "size_mm": [10.0, 6.0, 7.0], "center_mm": [-2.5, 4.0, 6.0], "rotation_deg": [-15.0, 0.0, 8.0]}, {"shape": "ellipsoid", "size_mm": [7.0, 5.0, 5.0], "center_mm": [4.0, 3.0, 5.0], "rotation_deg": [10.0, 0.0, 0.0]}]}}
